someone was asking about compiling nethack for OS/2 v2.

well, i just did it using the emx-gcc port.

here are some hints of what to do

1) pretend your on a UNIX machine ... emx-gcc provides a UNIX-like
view onto OS/2. -- btw its mainly a USG variant and not BSD

2) you'll need a -traditional and -fwritable-strings options to
gcc as in the make files

3) there are some #ifdef OS2's already in to cope with the strict
enforcement of the 8.3 filename rule.

4) change the "_lock"'s to ".lck" in topten.c to obey 8.3 filenames

5) in end.c and panic.c there are couple of (void) typecasts to
fix under #ifdef SYSV's

6) may be one or two other minor code glitches but there was nothing
major to be done.

7) if on a 386sx have patience while it compiles!

